Markora 2 Privacy Policy
Updated: November 7, 2026
Developer: Hu Dongsheng (胡冬生)
Contact: hudongsheng356@gmail.com

Local processing
Markora 2 is a local image annotation app. It reads images, JSON annotations, YOLO text, COCO JSON, Pascal VOC XML, and Core ML / ONNX models that you choose through the system file picker, and saves files in locations you authorize. Images, annotations, and model inference are processed on your Mac. The app does not upload them to the developer or third-party servers.

Data the app does not collect
The app includes no advertising, analytics SDKs, developer telemetry, or user tracking. It does not send images, annotations, device identifiers, or usage records to the developer. No separate Markora 2 account is required.

Subscriptions and Apple services
Subscription purchases, restoration and entitlement verification use Apple StoreKit and connect to the App Store. Purchases require an Apple Account. Apple processes payment and subscription information under its own policies; the developer does not receive your payment card details. The app checks verified subscription entitlements to determine access. These operations do not upload your images or annotations to the developer. Manage or cancel subscriptions in your Apple account settings.

Local storage
Edited annotations are saved as JSON beside images. Exports are written to your selected folder. Dataset imports create a new project and a source-file manifest. Batch rename backs up original JSON to .markora-backups in the image folder and records before/after hashes for recovery. Detection candidates are cached in .markora-candidates, including classes, coordinates, confidence, model name, and SHA-256 image/annotation fingerprints.
Imported Core ML models are compiled and copied; ONNX models are copied directly into Application Support/Markora/Models inside the app container. Model selection, interface language, and appearance preferences are stored locally.
These files are not sent to the developer. You can manage or delete them in Finder. Removing the app may not delete JSON or caches stored in your image folders.

Support
If you contact us by email, we receive your email address and the information you choose to send. We use it only to handle your support request and necessary follow-up. You do not need to provide original datasets or sensitive images. You may request deletion of support information through the same email address. Support email is processed by the email service used and is also subject to its policies.

System and third-party services
If you place files in iCloud or another synchronized folder, that service handles synchronization according to its settings; this is not an upload by Markora 2. Apple handles store purchases, downloads, and system diagnostics according to its policies and your settings. Markora 2 does not independently collect that information.

Permissions
The app uses the macOS sandbox and user-selected file read/write access. It does not request camera, microphone, location, or contacts access.

Changes and contact
We will update this policy if future versions change data handling. For privacy questions, contact Hu Dongsheng at hudongsheng356@gmail.com.
